    "description": "My main duties have been to enhance and maintain 3 of the major products of the Video Gaming Division.  \n1.\tSQLServer is a C# .NET Application implemented as a process and using .NET Remoting to communicate to up to hundreds of PC based Terminal Controllers which in turn control banks of Video Gaming Machines. Using various protocols (SAS, E2)  Various Directives are sent and Events received to enable total control and security of the network.  I worked on many extensions to the protocols such as Banner Message.  And on a major rewrite of Meter Anomaly processing which included packet level rejection.  Added CRC calculation classes for new protocol F3.  All Data Layer processing is done by this process using SQL Server Stored Procedures.  All of these modification entailed new modification to stored procedures which I wrote as well as the C# code.\n2.\tCommand and Control is an internet enabled Client Server Application whereby the end user controls his system.  It allows monitoring and modifying all the Venues and devices attached to it.  I worked on major enhancements such as Expected and Received CRC’s,  Meter Fetch reporting.  This included adding and modifying Winforms using VB.Net and modifying or adding Stored Procedures.\n3.\tVLCSManager is a web application which is presented as a series of menu-linked web pages and allows basic data entry and modification in setting up and maintaining our system.  It is written in ASP.NET and VB.NET.  I worked on the modification of several Webform pages as well as new and modified report queries using SQL Server and Crystal Reports.",
